    "['no synchronization', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'no synchronization', 'parent_command': ['set protocols bgp local-as [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set protocols bgp local-as [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nno synchronization\\n##\\n\\nFor Juniper, the equivalent BGP configuration would typically not require an explicit \"no synchronization\" command since Juniper\\'s BGP implementation doesn\\'t have the synchronization feature enabled by default (unlike Cisco\\'s legacy behavior). However, if you want to explicitly ensure synchronization is disabled in Juniper, you would use:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols bgp group <group-name> no-synchronize\\n##\\n\\nNote: The exact Juniper command may vary slightly depending on the Junos version and context. The above is the closest functional equivalent to Cisco\\'s \"no synchronization\" command.', 'trans_template': 'no synchronization'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols bgp group <group-name> no-synchronize', 'parent_command': ['set protocols bgp local-as [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set protocols bgp local-as [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nno synchronization\\n##\\n\\nFor Juniper, the equivalent BGP configuration would typically not require an explicit \"no synchronization\" command since Juniper\\'s BGP implementation doesn\\'t have the synchronization feature enabled by default (unlike Cisco\\'s legacy behavior). However, if you want to explicitly ensure synchronization is disabled in Juniper, you would use:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols bgp group <group-name> no-synchronize\\n##\\n\\nNote: The exact Juniper command may vary slightly depending on the Junos version and context. The above is the closest functional equivalent to Cisco\\'s \"no synchronization\" command.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols bgp group <group-name> no-synchronize'}]]": 1,
